#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064030 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f437192-3fd7-5be0-8add-e8b38339eea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{8x}}{8}+\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289114} {:answer/id #uuid "7051331b-9832-5d38-9313-dacb894e97ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{4}+\\frac{5{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115} {:answer/id #uuid "b48058c2-5346-5519-abbb-5bcf8354e302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289116} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b92c9b-f60c-56d1-afd4-919813dc0996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289117} {:answer/id #uuid "7373ec35-03b3-5775-897d-2e1f54523943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{8}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48058c2-5346-5519-abbb-5bcf8354e302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289116} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fb0546-a595-54c5-b395-d753ce6ff53f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a8cff6a-f726-5f01-b056-1c73c4cb34b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114288" :question/problem "$\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{8x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}-\\int \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{8x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a0088b-1923-5fdb-ada8-dbb91684be77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289121} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c2f046-0e1e-54bb-b647-df1e1bbac18c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289122} {:answer/id #uuid "02327162-99a5-5018-a182-2a304b5ce1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289123} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8148c3-1142-5af7-8bb5-d1aa9d1c6016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289124} {:answer/id #uuid "5840cb45-3abb-5479-8451-bbb65798a149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02327162-99a5-5018-a182-2a304b5ce1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289123} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfcb73e0-5c96-58fc-a6e5-c62cb4c5e84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22b47a5c-d440-5039-af24-74694e9daefc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
